          "docs": "Delete a file from a vector database"
        },
        {
          "info": {
            "name": "Get Vector Database Metadata Snapshot",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "GET",
            "url": "https://flow.seekr.com/v1/flow/vectordb/:database_id/metadata",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "database_id",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "apikey",
              "key": "Authorization",
              "value": "{{Authorization}}",
              "placement": "header"
            }
          },
          "docs": "Return the current metadata snapshot for a vector database.\n\nThe snapshot is automatically refreshed whenever an ingestion job completes or a\nfile is deleted from the database (both are best-effort and asynchronous, so the\nrefresh may briefly lag the change), and can be regenerated on demand via POST on\nthis path. A snapshot with no metadata returns 200 with `keys: []`. Returns 404 if\na snapshot has never been generated for this database."
        },
        {
          "info": {
            "name": "Generate Vector Database Metadata Snapshot",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "POST",
            "url": "https://flow.seekr.com/v1/flow/vectordb/:database_id/metadata",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "database_id",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path"
              }
            ],
            "auth": {
              "type": "apikey",
              "key": "Authorization",
              "value": "{{Authorization}}",
              "placement": "header"
            }
          },
          "docs": "Generate (or refresh) the metadata snapshot for a vector database.\n\nSamples up to 10,000 random chunks from the index, ranks the top 100 metadata keys\nby frequency, and for each key records the top 10 most common values along with an\ninferred type. The snapshot is stored in Postgres and returned by GET on this path.\n\nRetrying is safe — each call replaces the prior snapshot.\n\nErrors:\n- 422 if the vector database is not found.\n- 502 with `SnapshotGenerationFailed` if the ingestion service cannot p"
        },
        {
          "info": {
            "name": "Update Vector Database Metadata",
            "type": "http"
          },
          "http": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "url": "https://flow.seekr.com/v1/flow/vectordb/:database_id/metadata",
            "params": [
              {
                "name": "database_id",
                "value": "",
                "type": "path"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "type": "json",
              "data": "{}"
            },
            "auth": {
              "type": "apikey",
              "key": "Authorization",
              "value": "{{Authorization}}",
              "placement": "header"
            }
          },
          "docs": "Overwrite metadata on chunks within a vector database, targeted by file_ids or chunk_ids.\n\nThis operation is **destructive**: the provided `metadata` object **replaces** all existing\nmetadata on every targeted chunk. Previous metadata fields that are not included in the\nnew object are permanently removed.\n\nTo preserve existing fields, include them explicitly in the new `metadata` object.\n\n**Metadata constraints:**\n- Must be a flat object (no nested objects or arrays).\n- Values must be `string`, "
        }
      ]
    }
